# an allow counts only after a comment marker the file's extension uses: prose and data that quote the syntax hold none, and an unknown extension takes it anywhere
spec: Allows
args: --format terse
exit: 1
-- docs/guide.md --
Keep it with `necro-allow banned-word: a reason`, on the hit's line.

```python
x = 1  # necro-allow banned-word: shown in a fence
```
<!-- necro-allow no-such-rule: a real comment -->
-- notes/issues.jsonl --
{"note": "necro-allow banned-word: quoted in data"}
-- src/a.py --
x = "necro-allow banned-word: inside a string, before any comment"
-- src/b.ts --
const ok = 1; // necro-allow banned-word: nothing here
-- src/c.weird --
necro-allow no-such-rule: an unknown type takes it anywhere
-- @stdout --
docs/guide.md:6:6: necro/unused-allow the allow for no-such-rule suppresses nothing
src/b.ts:1:18: necro/unused-allow the allow for banned-word suppresses nothing
src/c.weird:1:1: necro/unused-allow the allow for no-such-rule suppresses nothing
